{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-355275",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nThe outputs are $5,$ $-2,$ $5,$ and $3,$ so the maximum output value is $5.$ This maximum occurs at both $x=-4$ and $x=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=5\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=\\{-4,3\\}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
